# Ejection checklist for {{KTM_CREATE_PROJECT_NAME}}

Eject/self-contained packaging is a future explicit flow, not a normal `ktm pack` mode today.

## Current expectation

- [ ] `ktm pack --mode compiled` succeeds without vendoring dependency closure.
- [ ] `ktm pack --mode compiled-source` succeeds without vendoring dependency closure.
- [ ] `ktm pack --mode eject` fails until KTM implements a reviewed eject flow.
- [ ] Normal archives do not contain `deps/`, `.ktrees/`, KTM store paths, or kt-node dependency libraries.

## SDK-specific risk

Python runtime source is packaged as the app artifact; ejecting would additionally vendor native kt-node dependency libraries and their licenses, which is not part of compiled or compiled-source mode.

## Before any future eject implementation

- [ ] Make eject an explicit command or mode with clear UX; do not silently overload `compiled-source`.
- [ ] Copy the full dependency closure deterministically into an owned payload root such as `deps/`.
- [ ] Include license notices and SBOM/provenance evidence for vendored dependencies.
- [ ] Document who owns security updates after ejection.
- [ ] Re-run native link audit against the self-contained closure.
- [ ] Add release tests proving compiled modes remain KTM-managed while eject mode vendors only the intended closure.
